    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p8-q25-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Prove that\n$$\\sin\\alpha=2\\sin\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\cos\\frac{\\alpha}{2}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sin\\alpha=2\\sin\\dfrac{\\alpha}{2}\\cos\\dfrac{\\alpha}{2}$.\n\nApply the sine double-angle identity with $\\theta=\\frac{\\alpha}{2}$.",
          "worked": "Using $\\sin 2\\theta=2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta$ with $\\theta=\\frac{\\alpha}{2}$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin\\alpha&=\\sin\\left(2\\cdot\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\right)\\\\\\sin\\alpha&=2\\sin\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\cos\\frac{\\alpha}{2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q25-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, prove that\n$$\\sin\\alpha=4\\sin\\frac{\\alpha}{4}\\cos\\frac{\\alpha}{4}\\cos\\frac{\\alpha}{2}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sin\\alpha=4\\sin\\dfrac{\\alpha}{4}\\cos\\dfrac{\\alpha}{4}\\cos\\dfrac{\\alpha}{2}$.\n\nApply part (a) to $\\sin(\\frac{\\alpha}{2})$.",
          "worked": "Apply part (a) again to the sine factor:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin\\alpha&=2\\sin\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\cos\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\\\\\sin\\alpha&=2\\left(2\\sin\\frac{\\alpha}{4}\\cos\\frac{\\alpha}{4}\\right)\\cos\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\\\\\sin\\alpha&=4\\sin\\frac{\\alpha}{4}\\cos\\frac{\\alpha}{4}\\cos\\frac{\\alpha}{2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q25-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "More generally, for $n\\in\\mathbb{N}$, deduce that\n$$\\sin\\alpha=2^n\\sin\\frac{\\alpha}{2^n}\\prod_{i=1}^{n}\\cos\\frac{\\alpha}{2^i}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sin\\alpha=2^n\\sin\\dfrac{\\alpha}{2^n}\\displaystyle\\prod_{i=1}^{n}\\cos\\dfrac{\\alpha}{2^i}$.\n\nRepeat part (a) on the remaining sine factor $n$ times; each substitution contributes a factor of $2$ and one cosine factor.",
          "worked": "Repeatedly apply part (a) to the remaining sine factor:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin\\alpha&=2\\sin\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\cos\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\\\\\sin\\alpha&=2^2\\sin\\frac{\\alpha}{2^2}\\cos\\frac{\\alpha}{2^2}\\cos\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\\\\\sin\\alpha&=2^3\\sin\\frac{\\alpha}{2^3}\\cos\\frac{\\alpha}{2^3}\\cos\\frac{\\alpha}{2^2}\\cos\\frac{\\alpha}{2}.\\end{align*}$$\nAfter $n$ substitutions, the sine argument is $\\frac{\\alpha}{2^n}$, the coefficient is $2^n$, and the cosine arguments are $\\frac{\\alpha}{2^i}$ for $i=1,\\ldots,n$. Hence\n$$\\sin\\alpha=2^n\\sin\\frac{\\alpha}{2^n}\\prod_{i=1}^{n}\\cos\\frac{\\alpha}{2^i}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      }
    ]
  },
